      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to calculate the total number of rounds played and divide it by the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see the following number of golfers:\n\n- 1 golfer played 1 round\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\n\\[\n1 \\text{ round} \\times 1 \\text{ golfer} + 2 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} + 3 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} + 4 \\text{ rounds} \\times 3 \\text{ golfers} + 5 \\text{ rounds} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 1 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 3 + 5 \\times 5\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 1 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 48 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\n\\[\n1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 13 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\nTo find the average number of rounds played per golfer, we divide the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{48 \\text{ rounds}}{13 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 3.6923\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.6923 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
